Comparison of Original and Stego Images

The original carrier image and the stego image were examined and compared using file size analysis, SHA-256 hash calculations, hexadecimal inspection with xxd, and string analysis. Although both images appeared visually identical when opened, their hash values were different because the stego image contained concealed information. This demonstrates how steganography can modify digital data without producing noticeable visual changes. The comparison successfully showed the difference between visual appearance and underlying binary content.
